{{ template "head" "Campfire Tools" }}
<div class="container index-landing">
    <div class="container-header">
        <h1>Campfire Tools</h1>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <p>
            Welcome to the Campfire Toolkit for Community Ambassadors. Each link in the navigation bar opens
            a purpose-built workflow pulled straight from the tools in this codebase, so you always know what
            to expect before you click.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>Raffle</h2>
        <p>
            Run quick giveaways by pasting one or more Campfire event links, picking how many winners you need,
            and choosing whether to limit entries to checked-in attendees or one entry per person. Past raffles
            are saved so you can review results or rerun them with a click.
        </p>
        <div class="buttons" hx-boost="true">
            <a href="/raffle" class="button">Open Raffle</a>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>Tracker</h2>
        <p>
            After logging in with Discord you can manage every club tied to your account: browse events,
            monitor members and check-ins, import or export data, run club-specific raffles, and hand out
            reward codes. It is the control room that powers the other tools.
        </p>
        <div class="buttons" hx-boost="true">
            <a href="/tracker/login" class="button">Go to Tracker</a>
        </div>
    </div>

        <div class="section">
        <h2>Export</h2>
        <p>
            Need spreadsheets for reporting? The export page lets you pull Campfire check-ins for specific
            events, choose exactly which columns to include, optionally merge every event into a single CSV,
            and even keep entries that Campfire doesn't name so nothing gets lost.
        </p>
        <div class="buttons" hx-boost="true">
            <a href="/export" class="button">Open Export</a>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>API Docs</h2>
        <p>
            Prefer automation? The API documentation spells out the <code>/api/events</code> export,
            club-specific endpoints, and the event import payloads, so you can script the same workflows
            without leaving your terminal.
        </p>
        <div class="buttons" hx-boost="true">
            <a href="/api/docs" class="button">View API Docs</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
{{ template "footer" }}
